    "title": "banken or auditd tampered with",
    "desc": "A program tried to stop, disable, remove or neuter the detection itself - the banken service, unit, timer or binary, or the audit daemon that feeds it. Impairing defenses (ATT&CK T1562) is a near-universal early step once an attacker has a foothold: kill the watchdog, then act unseen. A watchdog that cannot see itself being turned off is no watchdog, so this is deliberately broad and rated critical - a legitimate admin stop-for-maintenance will trip it too, and should be acknowledged rather than suppressed.",
